WEBVTT

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:08.179
Pentagon officials continue to deny any security breach and any responsibility for the events of Dark Thursday.

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:12.199
Experts predicted recovery from Dark Thursday would take years.

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:16.339
But here in Metropolis, the cleanup effort has been remarkably swift.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.199
The public is stunned in how fast rubble has been cleared from the streets.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.820
This is Genevieve Sparling reporting live from a...

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:27.000
You've been out again all night, having it?

00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:29.379
Can't do what I need to do in the daylight.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.200
Clark, I know you want to help.

00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:36.920
but you can't single-handedly rebuild everything that's been destroyed.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.219
It's my mess, Mom. I need to clean it up.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.460
You're not responsible for what happened. Zod is.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.320
Zod would not have been released.

00:00:47.119 --> 00:00:48.979
For once in my life, I'd listen to Jarrell.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.719
I've done what he asked me to do.

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:57.429
I have chores to do.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.600
Hey, are you okay?

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:04.959
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:01:05.359 --> 00:01:06.640
Clark, wait, wait, wait.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.239
I've never seen you this worn out.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.700
Even you have your limits.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.700
The chores can wait.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.700
I'm okay. Really? I'm fine.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:03:47.509
They think the school should reopen by next semester.

00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:50.509
It was nice of you to offer me a room with the national.

00:03:50.509 --> 00:03:52.509
I don't know what I would have done.

00:03:52.509 --> 00:04:02.560
If you're not okay with this and having second thoughts, then let's talk.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.729
Nothing to talk about. Everything's great.

00:04:07.729 --> 00:04:24.990
Clark, was that the first time you ever sneezed?

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:25.990
Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.990
The first time I've had a scratchy throat with my ears all plugged up.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:29.990
98.6.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:30.990
No fever.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.990
I'm no doctor, but it's not.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.990
It seems like it's just a common cold.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.990
You're far from common, Clark.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.990
I don't remember you ever even having the sniffles.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.990
I've never pushed myself so far into overdrive before.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.990
You know, you said when you were in that zone,

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:45.990
your powers were gone.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.990
That means your immune system was normal.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.990
You could have been exposed to something there.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.990
Whatever it is, I'm not really that sick.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:59.069
Hey, you guys are not going to believe what just happened to me.

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:02.069
I'm out there jogging along, minding my own business.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:05.069
When out of nowhere, a barn door comes following.

00:05:05.069 --> 00:05:07.069
from the clear blue sky and almost crushes me.

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:11.339
How does that happen?

00:05:11.339 --> 00:05:13.339
Maybe it fell from an airplane.

00:05:13.339 --> 00:05:17.339
Good guess, but the only thing up there was a severely traumatized sparrow.

00:05:17.339 --> 00:05:23.180
Uh-oh, does Clarkie have this? Nipples?

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.589
It's just a little cold.

00:05:26.589 --> 00:05:30.100
Lucky for you, I have the perfect remedy.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.100
Honey and a little bit of cayenne pepper.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.100
It works every time. First, it makes you sneeze a bunch of times,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.100
then I swear you're pretty much cured.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.100
You lost I'll pass.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.370
I think we're all out of cayenne Lois.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.370
Now you're not.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.370
I'm just gonna whip up a little bit of something here.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:51.680
Where do you?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.680
Where did your barn door go?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.680
It was here late last night when I came to drop off the documents,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.680
and now it's gone.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.680
Look at that. It is gone.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:05.439
And it's been ripped right off its hinges.

00:06:05.439 --> 00:06:07.439
Oh my god, that barn door. I knew it looked familiar.

00:06:07.439 --> 00:06:09.439
Now, how in the world does that happen?

00:06:09.439 --> 00:06:26.529
Mr. Pontius, what the hell am I paying you for?

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:28.529
I was followed again today.

00:06:28.529 --> 00:06:31.529
Black Range Rover, edge city plates.

00:06:31.529 --> 00:06:35.529
I tracked it to an abandoned factor on Fifth in Hayworth.

00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:36.529
Then why are you still still?

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:46.279
here. I'm on my way. I want this taken care of by any means necessary. Do you understand?

00:06:46.279 --> 00:06:57.019
I had no idea I was moving into a fortress.

00:06:57.019 --> 00:07:00.019
Wherever I turn, there's another security guard.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:07.370
Lana, that gentleman's not a security guard. He's a private investigator.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:13.540
Over the last few days, it's become clear I'm being followed.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.540
By who?

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:20.540
Oh, I doubt I had to look much further than the lowest branch in the family tree, but

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.540
I can't be sure.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.540
You called the police.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.540
After breaking every law imaginable and I was inhabited by Zod,

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.540
I don't want to go anywhere near a badge.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:36.579
I can't trust anyone, not even my own security.

00:07:36.579 --> 00:07:37.579
You can trust me.

00:07:37.579 --> 00:07:46.579
Then I want you to have this.

00:07:46.579 --> 00:07:50.569
Case of an emergency.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:55.579
He's the best PI in Metropolis.

00:07:55.579 --> 00:07:58.579
If anything happens to me, you need to call that number.

00:07:58.579 --> 00:08:02.579
Not the police. Robert Pontius will make sure you're safe.

00:08:02.579 --> 00:08:21.290
Lex, don't talk like that.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.290
Chloe.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.290
How's this for a mega-dose of guilt money?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.290
Excuse me.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:30.290
Yeah, well, um, I've got bigger news.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.289
What happened? Is everything alright?

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:35.860
I sneezed.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:39.289
And?

00:08:39.289 --> 00:08:40.289
And?

00:08:40.289 --> 00:08:41.289
Chloe, that's not normal.

00:08:41.289 --> 00:08:44.289
Well, Clark, nothing with you is exactly normal,

00:08:44.289 --> 00:08:46.289
but I wouldn't call sneezing today's headline.

00:08:46.289 --> 00:08:48.289
You don't understand. I...

00:08:48.289 --> 00:08:49.289
I...

00:08:49.289 --> 00:08:50.289
I...

00:08:50.289 --> 00:08:53.289
You what? Grab a tissue and get over it.

00:08:53.289 --> 00:09:02.940
Kuzintite.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.500
I tried to warn you, I've come down with some sort of cold.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.500
And become a walking air cannon.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.500
Clark, let's get you out of here before we glow again.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.500
At least I was able to cover half my face that time this morning.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.500
I blew the barn door halfway across Lowell County.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.500
It almost hit Lois.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.500
Lois is in Lane?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.500
Now she's on a one-woman crusade to find an explanation.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.500
You know her, she won't stop digging until she hits China.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.500
Yeah, okay, I'll take care of Lois.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.500
You just take care of that cold.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.500
We have enough natural disasters around here

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.500
without having to worry about hurrying Clark looming off the coast.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.500
No!

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:37.620
Just kidding.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:54.090
Well, I forgot what a concerned parent you are.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.090
That's why you're having me followed, isn't it?

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.090
To make sure I don't destroy the rest of the world?

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:03.090
If I were having you followed, son, you would never know it.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.090
I can guarantee you that.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:07.090
I hate to disappoint you, but whatever powers I had are long gone.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:10.090
So if you're looking for an encore performance, you're out of luck.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.090
Elvis has left the building.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.090
Yeah. You want to find out who's stalking you?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:19.090
I suggest you concentrate on remembering every little, minute detail of that horrific...

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.090
of that horrific day.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:24.090
Well, I guess I should have kept a blog.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:27.090
Because I suffered a total memory loss.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:30.090
Besides what Lana has told me, those 24 hours are gone.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:36.860
They could have been witnessed by anyone.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.860
Lex, please, let me help you.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.860
I've been on the receiving end of your help before, Dad.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.860
I think I'll pass.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.960
Listen to me.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.960
There are some adversaries that cannot be defeated alone.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.139
Lex! Lex!

00:10:54.139 --> 00:10:55.139
Lex!

00:10:55.139 --> 00:11:40.009
Bears hibernating.

00:11:40.009 --> 00:11:41.009
It's over.

00:11:41.009 --> 00:11:55.259
How you doing?

00:11:55.259 --> 00:11:59.259
This is one part about being human I don't envy.

00:11:59.259 --> 00:12:01.259
It's not all that bad.

00:12:01.259 --> 00:12:06.259
You can lie on the couch all day and watch DVDs while your mom makes some doctor-certified chicken soup.

00:12:06.259 --> 00:12:10.259
Mom, I can watch DVDs after I fix the irrigation ditch.

00:12:10.259 --> 00:12:13.259
No, your health is a lot more important than the irrigation ditch.

00:12:13.259 --> 00:12:18.259
You're in uncharted waters now, Clark, and your dad's not here to help us out.

00:12:18.259 --> 00:12:22.259
So, please, you have to trust my instincts and rest.

00:12:22.259 --> 00:12:31.779
Is everything all right?

00:12:31.779 --> 00:12:32.779
Lex.

00:12:32.779 --> 00:12:35.279
He's gone. I think he's been abducted.

00:12:35.279 --> 00:12:39.679
Who do you think is behind it?

00:12:39.679 --> 00:12:43.309
I, considering what he stole from the Pentagon,

00:12:43.309 --> 00:12:46.309
my initial reaction, was the, uh, government.

00:12:46.309 --> 00:12:49.809
But, uh, after I spoke to my contacts in Washington, I don't think so.

00:12:49.809 --> 00:12:50.809
I...

00:12:50.809 --> 00:12:53.809
You have to find him, Clark.

00:12:53.809 --> 00:12:56.809
Why? Lex and I have nothing to do with each other anymore.

00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:58.809
But you and Zod do.

00:12:58.809 --> 00:13:04.080
Lex insists he can't remember anything that happened

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.080
when he was possessed by Zod, but, uh, he might not be honest about it.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.080
He might remember.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.080
at all.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:14.080
Whoever his captors are, if they put enough pressure on him,

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.080
he could tell the truth about you.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:37.679
Now, good morning, Mr. Invincible.

00:13:37.679 --> 00:13:41.980
Where am I?

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:45.980
In your cage, where every lab rat belongs?

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:46.980
Oh, and...

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.980
Before you even try escaping, you might want to consider

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:52.980
you're hooked up to enough waters to drop an elephant.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.980
Who are you?

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.980
Just someone who's interested in how you possess superhuman powers.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:58.980
Human Powers.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:07.100
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:09.100
Oh, come on, Lex!

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:15.100
We both know you were the one at the Pentagon, swatting away those bullets like they were mosquitoes,

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:18.100
and not even a scratch.

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:23.100
Yeah, see, we saw it on the only working satellite on Dark Thursday.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:27.100
So, we know you have the powers.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:30.100
Just kind of want to know how you got them.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.100
My people are already on to you.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.100
Your people.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:40.480
I think that's the guy caught kind of roaming around outside.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.480
Ponies, right?

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:48.200
The guy downstairs with a bullet in his hand.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.200
Enough for play. All right?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.200
Let's get this started.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.200
You're gonna tell me everything.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:15:09.649
See, I told you I am no chicken little and that is no acorn.

00:15:09.649 --> 00:15:11.649
Whoa.

00:15:11.649 --> 00:15:13.649
Now, how is that even remotely conceivable?

00:15:13.649 --> 00:15:15.649
The kents live miles away from me.

00:15:15.649 --> 00:15:17.649
Okay, it's definitely weird. I'll give you that,

00:15:17.649 --> 00:15:18.649
but it's not wall of wall of walt.

00:15:18.649 --> 00:15:20.649
It's called a microburst.

00:15:20.649 --> 00:15:22.649
A micro what?

00:15:22.649 --> 00:15:24.649
It's like a sudden, mini-tornado.

00:15:24.649 --> 00:15:27.649
It happens when there are extreme changes in the temperature.

00:15:27.649 --> 00:15:29.649
It's actually not that unheard of in the Midwest.

00:15:29.649 --> 00:15:32.649
It was sunny in 75. There was nothing extreme about the weather.

00:15:32.649 --> 00:15:34.649
Well, you might not have felt it.

00:15:34.649 --> 00:15:36.649
I mean, it was probably in the upper atmosphere,

00:15:36.649 --> 00:15:40.649
but there must have been some sort of change in the barometric pressures.

00:15:40.649 --> 00:15:44.649
Okay, either you've been watching little too much weather channel

00:15:44.649 --> 00:15:47.649
or a year at the Daily Planet has turned you into a hardened skeptic.

00:15:47.649 --> 00:15:48.649
It's called being realistic.

00:15:48.649 --> 00:15:50.649
Lois, you might want to try it once in a while?

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:55.649
You were the one who always told me that science can explain only a fraction of what happens in this crazy town.

00:15:55.649 --> 00:15:57.649
And this happens to fall into that fraction.

00:15:57.649 --> 00:15:59.649
Look, Lois, I still believe in the paranormal.

00:15:59.649 --> 00:16:00.649
Trust me.

00:16:00.649 --> 00:16:04.649
But you have to accept the fact that sometimes the answers you're looking for

00:16:04.649 --> 00:16:07.649
are no further away than the front pages of your scientific American.

00:16:07.649 --> 00:16:22.870
What are you doing with the gun?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:25.870
We were specifically told not to use violence.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.870
So?

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.870
I don't answer to anybody, okay? Especially your boss.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:35.870
And what I want to know is how bullets bounced off his body like ping pong balls.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:39.870
Information like that is very valuable on the open market.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:43.539
You were specifically hired to...

00:16:43.539 --> 00:16:45.539
Yeah, well, guess what?

00:16:45.539 --> 00:16:47.539
I'm an entrepreneur, okay?

00:16:47.539 --> 00:16:52.539
So either you join my newest venture or you can end up like the Pontius guy.

00:16:52.539 --> 00:16:54.539
Your choice.

00:16:54.539 --> 00:17:04.059
Hey, Lex! Yeah, I was thinking.

00:17:04.059 --> 00:17:07.059
Why don't we try a little experiment?

00:17:07.059 --> 00:17:09.059
What are you doing?

00:17:09.059 --> 00:17:12.059
I told you I don't remember any of it happening.

00:17:12.059 --> 00:17:14.059
Yeah, but it did.

00:17:14.059 --> 00:17:16.059
And I want to see it happen again.

00:17:16.059 --> 00:17:17.059
Please, no.

00:17:17.059 --> 00:17:18.059
No.

00:17:18.059 --> 00:17:22.059
Ah! Oh, God!

00:17:22.059 --> 00:17:43.619
What are you doing here?

00:17:43.619 --> 00:17:47.619
I wanted to personally hand-deliver this article to your editor.

00:17:47.619 --> 00:17:49.619
An article. You're a journalist now?

00:17:49.619 --> 00:17:50.619
Yeah.

00:17:50.619 --> 00:17:54.619
Wow. That's a lot of words.

00:17:54.619 --> 00:17:57.619
While the Smallville ledger was way too small-minded, to appreciate

00:17:57.619 --> 00:18:01.619
investigative reportage, so I thought the planet would be the perfect publisher.

00:18:01.619 --> 00:18:05.619
Lois, I hate to be the one to rain on your Pulitzer parade,

00:18:05.619 --> 00:18:10.619
but I really don't think that a story about weather is going to stand a chance

00:18:10.619 --> 00:18:12.619
when we're still dealing with the aftermath of Dark Thursday.

00:18:12.619 --> 00:18:16.619
No, this story is way more than about wild weather, okay?

00:18:16.619 --> 00:18:19.619
Not only is it an expozy on the paranormal,

00:18:19.619 --> 00:18:22.619
it is a story about human triumph over adversity.

00:18:22.619 --> 00:18:24.619
That barn door could have chopped me in half. Read it.

00:18:24.619 --> 00:18:26.619
Funny, I don't remember there being an evening.

00:18:26.619 --> 00:18:28.619
Remember there being an E in Tornado.

00:18:28.619 --> 00:18:30.619
Just a little typo.

00:18:30.619 --> 00:18:32.619
And the extra H in weather?

00:18:32.619 --> 00:18:34.619
You know what I think?

00:18:34.619 --> 00:18:36.619
I think that you're just a little bit jealous

00:18:36.619 --> 00:18:39.619
that you're not the only one in the family with a natural way with words.

00:18:39.619 --> 00:18:42.619
Really? Well, Lowe, you know, you're right.

00:18:42.619 --> 00:18:46.619
I might be jealous of you, but words have nothing to do with it.

00:18:46.619 --> 00:18:48.619
Fine. Forget the Daily Planet.

00:18:48.619 --> 00:18:51.619
I don't need this stuffy, pseudo-intellectual rag.

00:18:51.619 --> 00:18:55.619
Out there somewhere is a newspaper that knows a story when they see one.

00:18:55.619 --> 00:18:56.619
Well, well...

00:18:56.619 --> 00:18:58.619
Good luck. Thank you.

00:18:58.619 --> 00:19:26.640
Anna, what are you doing here?

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.640
Actually, I'm living here now.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:33.269
You're looking for Lex. He's not here.

00:19:33.269 --> 00:19:34.269
Lex has gone missing.

00:19:34.269 --> 00:19:37.269
I think he may have been kidnapped.

00:19:37.269 --> 00:19:42.019
Oh God.

00:19:42.019 --> 00:19:47.990
Is he mentioned any recent threats against him?

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:48.990
Mauna, if you have any information,

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.990
that might be able to help me find him.

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:52.990
I don't understand, Clark.

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:56.990
Why are you the leader of his search party?

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.990
Lana, no matter what my differences are with Lex.

